Hi Jeanne,

Thanks for the note. You are correct that it is not possible to directly include species-specific traits/covariates into msPGOcc or any multi-species functions in spOccupancy. There are two alternative strategies I would suggest:
You could use the postHocLM() function <https://doserlab.com/files/spoccupancy-web/reference/posthoclm> to quantify relationships with species-traits after fitting the model. Basically, you would extract species-specific estimates from msPGOcc, then use those in a subsequent linear model that would relate those estimates to species-specific traits, while fully taking into account uncertainty. This is sort of a work around for not being able to fit species-specific traits directly in the spOccupancy model.
If you aren't planning to explore any of the spatial functionality in spOccupancy and you don't mind leaving the Bayesian framework, you can fit a multi-species occupancy model with species traits in unmarked using the relatively new occuComm  <https://cran.r-project.org/web/packages/unmarked/vignettes/occuComm.html>function in unmarked.
Kind regards,

Jeff

